  "description": "HALHAG crystallizes in the orthorhombic crystal system with space group P c c n. Reported CIF formula moiety: C96 H144 Cu8 Gd4 N8 O40 4+,4(Cl1 O4 1-),7(C1 H4 O1),3(H2 O1). From the CIF bond table, Gd1 (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Gd2 (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Gd3 (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Cu1 (Cu) has 4 O neighbors; Cu2 (Cu) has 4 O neighbors; Cu3 (Cu) has 4 O neighbors; Cu4 (Cu) has 4 O neighbors; Gd4 (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Cu5 (Cu) has 4 O neighbors; Cu6 (Cu) has 4 O neighbors; Cu7 (Cu) has 4 O neighbors; Cu8 (Cu) has 4 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 24 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.180-3.963 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 94.75-112.14°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Gd4Cu8(OH)8(Hpdm)8(O2CtBu)8](ClO4)4. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 8 OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 8 OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
